","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twobitadder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twobitadder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twobitadder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twobitadder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T14:31:12Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T14:31:12Z","body":"ah, well, alas, i'm really banking on embedded subwindows, so i don't think this is actually a workable solution. i tried it out and i had to set the `always_on_top` property as well to keep them from being covered by the main window when it took focus back, which also prevented marking the windows as `transient`. i'll continue playing around with some settings to see if i can find something to work, and i appreciate the assistance regardless!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239305665/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]